WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.770
Whether it’s a wild celebration, a somber
mourning or the season finale of The Bachelor,

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.610
hitting the bottle is not uncommon.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:12.150
What’s a bit more unusual, though, is getting
your drink on at your place of work.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.970
At most jobs, this is a big no-no, but in
Hollywood, things are a little different.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:24.740
"This is equal parts scotch, absinthe, rum,
gin, vermouth, triple sec, and 2 packs of

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:25.740
splenda."

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.689
Whether it inspired great performances or
caused some disastrous behind the scenes drama,

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:34.320
here are some stories of actors who were drunk
during filming.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.070
"drink, l'chaim, to life!"

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.590
Denise Richards and Neve Campbell

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.469
It doesn't matter who you are: if you find
yourself kissing a girl for the first time

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:49.710
in your life, naked in a pool, surrounded
by a film crew — a cocktail...or five...might

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:50.710
be in order.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.530
That was definitely the case for actresses
Neve Campbell and Denise Richards who needed

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.539
some liquid courage before filming their famously
steamy scene from Wild Things.

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:03.660
This was going to be the first time either
of the actresses had kissed a girl before,

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.650
so they decided to take the edge off by pounding
back an entire pitcher of margaritas before

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.490
the camera started rolling.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:14.569
Looking back on the kiss now, Campbell said
it was actually pretty fun and that they were

00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:17.609
definitely thankful for the pre-filming drink.

00:01:17.609 --> 00:01:19.569
Daniel Radcliffe

00:01:19.569 --> 00:01:24.439
By the time Daniel Radcliffe turned 18 and
was filming his sixth Harry Potter movie,

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:26.929
he found himself quite lost in the drink.

00:01:26.929 --> 00:01:32.009
What started out as a fun lifestyle of partying
quickly degenerated into a serious problem

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:35.619
that found Radcliffe blacking out multiple
times per week.

00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:40.149
The actor did his best to keep some distance
between his work and his drinking and he maintains

00:01:40.149 --> 00:01:43.399
that he never actually drank on the Harry
Potter set.

00:01:43.399 --> 00:01:47.899
Radcliffe has admitted, however, that he often
would show up in the morning still drunk from

00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:52.270
the night before, and would start shooting
while clearly still under the influence.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:56.899
The actor claims he can tell which scenes
he was inebriated for, but he's understandably

00:01:56.899 --> 00:01:59.630
refused to share that information with the
public.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:04.579
The only solution to this predicament: set
aside a weekend and have yourself an eagle-eyed

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:09.099
Harry Potter movie marathon...and maybe a
few drinks too.

00:02:09.099 --> 00:02:10.099
Robert Shaw

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:13.860
It’s no secret that actor Robert Shaw liked
to drink.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:18.260
And as it turns out, this affinity for the
bottle affected the actor’s famous performance

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.569
in 1975’s Jaws.

00:02:20.569 --> 00:02:25.450
Before filming a particularly tricky monologue,
Shaw asked director Steven Spielberg if he

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.129
could have a bit to drink to help him loosen
up.

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:32.590
Unfortunately, that "bit to drink" resulted
in Shaw showing up to the shoot completely

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:33.590
wasted.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.510
The actor was unable to perform the scene
and ruined the entire shoot for the day.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:42.230
The next day, Shaw showed up to set with his
tail between his legs and was very apologetic

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:43.510
for the way he acted.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:47.540
Spielberg forgave him, Shaw knocked the scene
out of the park.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:53.860
"Y’know, the thing about a shark, he’s
got lifeless eyes, black eyes, like a doll’s

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:54.820
eyes."

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.980
And the rest is history.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.480
Martin Sheen

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.420
Of all the famous film shoots in the history
of Hollywood, perhaps none are quite as legendary

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.390
as the set of Apocalypse Now.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.890
Leading man Martin Sheen was a late addition
to the film, and when he arrived, he found

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.689
a set in chaos.

00:03:11.689 --> 00:03:15.510
Needless to say, he wasted no timing diving
right into the thick of it.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:20.129
Apparently, director Francis Ford Coppola
kept Sheen locked up and completely hammered

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:24.959
for days on end in an effort to get the emotionally
driven performance he was looking for.

00:03:24.959 --> 00:03:29.090
Coppola even toyed with Sheen’s psyche,
telling the actor that the rest of the production

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:31.340
team was evil and out to get him.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:35.569
The performance ended up being pretty amazing,
but it sounds like Martin Sheen went through

00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:38.299
a drunken hell to get there.

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:39.590
Margot Robbie

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:44.200
Australian-born actress Margot Robbie is one
of the most sought after actresses working

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.200
today.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.000
Still, her big break might never have happened
if it weren't for a helpful crew member who

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.610
happened to have some booze on hand.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:55.220
On the set of The Wolf of Wall Street, Robbie
had to bare all, and the actress was very

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.969
nervous for the nude moment.

00:03:56.969 --> 00:04:00.139
She knew eventually she'd watch that scene
with her dear mum.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:04.859
"I actually tried to cover her eyes when the
nude bits happened, but she pushed my hand

00:04:04.859 --> 00:04:05.859
away."

00:04:05.859 --> 00:04:10.950
Luckily, a member of the production team offered
Robbie some tequila to help her calm her nerves.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.130
She quickly threw back three shots and was
ready to roll.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:19.199
The scene turned out great and Robbie credits
the booze for helping her nail the R-rated

00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:20.199
moment.

00:04:20.199 --> 00:04:22.060
Brad Pitt and Edward Norton

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:26.330
Despite how tight the script seemed, there
were several improvised moments during the

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.520
filming of Fight Club.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.040
"Mother f***er!

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.300
You hit me in the ear."

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:40.120
On top of that improvised hit, the scene in
which Brad Pitt and Ed Norton drunkenly smack

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.620
golf balls from their house was also unplanned
— and surprisingly method.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:49.030
The actors, who had bonded on set, had actually
gotten drunk together and started smacking

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.530
golf balls at the film’s catering trucks.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:55.620
When Fincher saw them, he thought it fit their
rebellious characters, and decided to roll

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:56.620
the cameras.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:01.060
Pitt remembers the drunken sequence fondly,
and this honest moment of bonding not only

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:05.270
helped the actors get closer but actually
gave birth to one of the more popular scenes

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:06.740
from the film.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.280
Peter O'Toole and Omar Sharif

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.950
The late Peter O'Toole was almost as famous
for his drinking as he was for his acting.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:18.169
By the time the actor’s starring role in
Lawrence of Arabia came about, he was already

00:05:18.169 --> 00:05:23.349
well versed in the art of on-set drinking,
and he decided it was time to spread the wealth.

00:05:23.349 --> 00:05:28.229
During the famous Aqaba scene, O’Toole’s
co-star, Omar Sharif, was terrified of falling

00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:32.009
off his camel and he considered tying his
legs to the animal.

00:05:32.009 --> 00:05:34.199
But O’Toole had a different plan in mind.

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:38.169
He suggested that they ought to just get drunk
and let the rest work itself out.

00:05:38.169 --> 00:05:42.259
Sharif obliged, and the two proceeded to get
sloshed on brandy and milk.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:48.139
O'Toole and Sharif ended up delivering some
of the most famous performances in film history.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:52.020
"Thank you, alcohol."

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.200
Thanks for watching!

